{
  "title": "Introduction — argument graph",
  "section": "introduction",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "role": "opening",
      "point": "Damage travels as a chain and is governed by the water state, not the rainfall anomaly"
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "role": "middle",
      "point": "Monitoring resolves the deficit and not the impact state"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "role": "middle",
      "point": "Forecasts of the deficit are not forecasts of the damage"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "role": "middle",
      "point": "Impact depends on when and where the deficit lands, and is thresholded"
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "role": "middle",
      "point": "Onset speed is a second dimension, and its definition is unsettled"
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "role": "closing",
      "point": "Open question: connect forecast water states to impact thresholds"
    }
  ],
  "nodes": [
